<h1>Serbian Subcategorization  Grammar for Natural Language Generation</h1>Version of September 11, 2026, 2:06 pm<br />Documentation available at <a href="http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar" target="_blank">http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar</a><br />Tagset available at <a href="../dictionary/export_tagset.php" target="_blank">Export UNDL Foundation tagset</a>.<br /><br /><b>Y0</b><br />AVALENT<br /><br /><b>Y1</b><br />NO SUBCATEGORIZATION FRAME: rules defined inside the entry in the dictionary<br /><br /><b>Y40</b><br />Instransitive verbs (<i>umreti</i>)<br />VS(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y41</b><br />Transitive direct (<i>kupiti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC);<br /><br /><b>Y42</b><br />Ditransitive verbs whose indirect object is in genitive, and is introduced with a preposition od. (<i>štititi</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PH([od]));<br /><br /><b>Y43</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object is in instrumental, and is introduced with a preposition za. (<i>žudeti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([za];NP,INS));<br /><br /><b>Y45</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object is in locative, and is introduced with a preposition u. (<i>istrajati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([u];NP,LOC)); <br /><br /><b>Y49</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is in locative, and is introduced with a preposition o. (<i>informisati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([o];NP,LOC));<br /><br /><b>Y50</b><br />Pronominal intransitive verbs whose se can be analysed as reflexive pronoun sebe. (<i>češljati se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(FPR);<br /><br /><b>Y54</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object is in accusative, and is introduced with a preposition na.
 (<i>ciljati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([na];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y55</b><br />Ditransitive verbs with a direct object in accusative, and indirect in dative. (<i>dati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(NP,DAT);<br /><br /><b>Y59</b><br />Transitive verbs with indirect object in dative introduced with a preposition na. (<i>insistirati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([na];NP,DAT));<br /><br /><b>Y62</b><br />Ditransitive verbs whose indirect object in accusative is introduced with a preposition na. (<i>podsetiti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([na];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y63</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object is in dative. (<i>pretiti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,DAT);<br /><br /><b>Y64</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object in instrumental is introduced with a preposition s. (<i>pričati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([s];NP,INS));<br /><br /><b>Y65</b><br />Ditransitive verbs whose one object is in dative, and the other in accusative introduced with a preposition na. (<i>ukazati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,DAT)VC(PC([na];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y67</b><br />Ditransitive verbs whose indirect object in accusative is introduced with a preposition za. (<i>zamoliti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([za];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y69</b><br />Indirect transitive verbs whose object is in genitive. (<i>dočepati se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,GEN);<br /><br /><b>Y71</b><br />Ditransitive verbs whose indirect object is in instrumental. (<i>načiniti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(NP,INS);<br /><br /><b>Y72</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object is in instrumental. (<i>sladiti se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,INS);<br /><br /><b>Y75</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object in accusative is introduced with a preposition za. (<i>srepeti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([za];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y77</b><br />Transitive verbs whose object in accusative is introduced with a preposition u. (<i>pretvoriti se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC([u];NP,ACC);<br /><br /><b>Y79</b><br />Verbs whose indirect object is introduced with a preposition o and is in locative. (<i>razmišljati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([o];NP,LOC));<br /><br /><b>Y81</b><br />Transitive verbs whose indirect object is introduced with a preposition od. (<i>zavisiti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PH([od]));<br /><br /><b>Y82</b><br />Ditransitive verbs whose both objects are in accusative. (<i>učiti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(NP,ACC);<br /><br /><b>Y87</b><br />Verbs that take a clause as a complement. (<i>verovati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(CH([da]));<br /><br /><b>Y88</b><br />Ditransitive verbs whose indirect object is introduced by a preposition u followed by a noun in locative. (<i>pobediti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([u];NP,LOC));<br /><br /></body>
